[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Sign It with Flowsta Vault
GenericName=Cryptographically sign a file
Comment=Sign a file using your Flowsta Vault identity
Exec=flowsta-vault %F
Icon=flowsta-vault
Terminal=false
Categories=Utility;Security;
StartupWMClass=flowsta-vault
NoDisplay=true
# MIME types this app offers to sign — this is what adds "Sign It with
# Flowsta Vault" to the file manager's right-click "Open With" list.
#
# A .desktop MimeType entry does two things at once: it lists the app in
# "Open With" AND makes it eligible to become the DEFAULT opener for a
# type when it is the ONLY app registered for it (GNOME/Nautilus promote a
# sole registrant to default). So we DELIBERATELY EXCLUDE:
#   - application/octet-stream — the catch-all every unrecognized file
#     falls back to; registering it made Vault the default handler for
#     essentially every file on Linux.
#   - structured-data + source types (json, xml, text/xml, text/markdown,
#     text/x-python, text/x-rust, text/x-go, text/javascript) — a dev box
#     often has no other registered handler, so Vault would silently
#     become their default too.
# Every type kept below has an established system handler, so Vault only
# ever appears as a secondary "Open With" choice and never hijacks a default.
MimeType=application/pdf;application/rtf;application/zip;application/x-tar;application/gzip;application/x-7z-compressed;application/x-rar-compressed;application/msword;application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document;application/vnd.ms-excel;application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet;application/vnd.ms-powerpoint;application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation;application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.text;application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.spreadsheet;application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.presentation;text/plain;text/csv;text/html;image/png;image/jpeg;image/gif;image/bmp;image/tiff;image/webp;image/svg+xml;image/heic;image/heif;audio/mpeg;audio/mp4;audio/wav;audio/x-wav;audio/flac;audio/ogg;audio/webm;audio/x-m4a;video/mp4;video/x-matroska;video/quicktime;video/webm;video/x-msvideo;video/mpeg;video/x-flv;
